      "id": 1,
      "text": "Reverend Andreas Iverson founded Ephraim in 1853 as a Moravian religious community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ephraim%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Ephraim is known for its white buildings, shoreline along Green Bay, and views of the bluffs across Eagle Harbor.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ephraim%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Until 2016, Ephraim was the only dry municipality in the state of Wisconsin, prohibiting all alcohol sales and manufacture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ephraim%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The cultural and historical heritage of Ephraim is a blend of Moravian culture and Norwegian ethnic heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://ephraim.wi.gov/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The steeples of the Moravian and Free Evangelical Lutheran churches serve as the primary landmarks of Ephraim when seen from Eagle Harbor.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ephraim%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Ephraim maintains strict zoning laws to preserve the distinctive atmosphere and historic character of the village.",
